  {
   "evidence": "Physlib `Vector/Basic.lean:414` defines `ofTemporalComponent t = t \u2022 basis (Sum.inl 0)`; `timeComponent_basis_sum_inl` (line 389) and `spatialPart_basis_sum_inl` (line 348) already give the two primitives immediately, and `apply_sub` (line 150) / `apply_smul` (line 142) are `@[simp]`. BasicExtensions.lean:53 and :60 instead call `simp [ofTemporalComponent, basis_apply]` on the composite.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Causality/BasicExtensions.lean",
   "fix": "Add the two primitives `@[simp] lemma timeComponent_ofTemporalComponent (t : \u211d) : (ofTemporalComponent t : Vector d).timeComponent = t` and `@[simp] lemma spatialPart_ofTemporalComponent (t : \u211d) : (ofTemporalComponent t : Vector d).spatialPart = 0`, then get both current lemmas by `simp` (via Physlib's simp lemma `apply_sub`), and state the spatial one as `(v - ofTemporalComponent t).spatialPart = v.spatialPart`.",
   "issue": "`timeComponent_sub_ofTemporalComponent` (line 51) and `spatialPart_sub_ofTemporalComponent` (line 57) each unfold `ofTemporalComponent` and `basis_apply` for the special instance `v - ofTemporalComponent v.timeComponent`, while the general facts they rest on \u2014 `(ofTemporalComponent t : Vector d).timeComponent = t` and `(ofTemporalComponent t).spatialPart = 0` \u2014 exist nowhere (grep of `upstream/Physlib` finds `ofTemporalComponent` only at its definition, `Vector/Basic.lean:414`, and at use sites; no component lemmas). `spatialPart_sub_ofTemporalComponent` is additionally specialized for no reason: it holds for `v - ofTemporalComponent t` with any `t`. The resulting API is unusable for any later `ofTemporalComponent` computation (e.g. 0.3's boundary-point work) without re-unfolding the definition, and it is this composite shape that forces the simp-normal-form caveat in the line 47 docstring.",
   "line": 51
  }
 ],
